.TH "vsearch-fastq_stats" "1" "April 29, 2026" "version 2.31.0" "vsearch manual"
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
vsearch --fastq_stats \[em] analyze fastq sequences and output detailed
statistics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]vsearch\f[R] \f[B]--fastq_stats\f[R] \f[I]fastqfile\f[R] --log
\f[I]outputfile\f[R] [\f[I]options\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The vsearch command \f[V]--fastq_stats\f[R] analyzes fastq sequences and
outputs five detailed statistics tables, including projections of the
impact different filtering thresholds would have.
The statistics tables are described below, with an example for each.
Results are written to \f[V]--log\f[R] \f[I]outputfile\f[R].
The quality encoding of the input fastq and the range of accepted
quality values can be specified with \f[V]--fastq_ascii\f[R],
\f[V]--fastq_qmin\f[R] and \f[V]--fastq_qmax\f[R].
.SS Read length distribution (table 1)
.PP
Observed read lengths are sorted in decreasing order.
The largest length value is marked with `>='.
.IP "1." 3
L: read length
.IP "2." 3
N: number of reads
.IP "3." 3
Pct: fraction of reads with this length
.IP "4." 3
AccPct: fraction of reads with this length or longer
.IP
