.SS Effect of expected error and length filtering (table 4)
.PP
Positions in reads are sorted in decreasing order, starting with the
first read length (L) with a cummulated expected error smaller or equal
to 1.0.
The next four columns indicate the number of reads that would be
retained by the command \f[V]vsearch-fastq_filter(1)\f[R] if the reads
were truncated at length L with the option \f[V]--fastq_trunclen\f[R],
and filtered to have a maximum expected error equal to or lesser than
1.0, 0.5, 0.25 or 0.1 with the option \f[V]--fastq_maxee\f[R].
The last four columns indicate the fraction of reads that would be
retained by the command \f[V]vsearch-fastq_filter(1)\f[R] using the same
length L and maximum expected error parameters.
.IP "1." 3
L: read length
.IP "2." 3
number of reads if truncating at L and filtering at EE =< 1.0
.IP "3." 3
number of reads if truncating at L and filtering at EE =< 0.5
.IP "4." 3
number of reads if truncating at L and filtering at EE =< 0.25
.IP "5." 3
number of reads if truncating at L and filtering at EE =< 0.1
.IP "6." 3
fraction of reads if truncating at L and filtering at EE =< 1.0
.IP "7." 3
fraction of reads if truncating at L and filtering at EE =< 0.5
.IP "8." 3
fraction of reads if truncating at L and filtering at EE =< 0.25
.IP "9." 3
fraction of reads if truncating at L and filtering at EE =< 0.1
.IP
